  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Climate Just Communities Rwanda</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In line with climate justice principles and the pillars of climate justice, the Climate Just Communities programme takes a community-led, participatory approach to building climate resilience and inclusivity in communities. By embedding human rights and a commitment to gender equality, disability, and social inclusion, it empowers vulnerable groups to lead climate action tailored to their needs. This activity entry is the Scottish Government&apos;s CJC programme in Rwanda delivered via a contract with SCIAF.</narrative>
  </description>
